{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review BLOCK remediation (2026-08-10, origin/main 4f5bc5e89c): confirmed four material gaps. Current `search --output json` is hard-rejected as an unknown option; it is not absorbed into the query. `list` already drops bodies by default through `include_body=False`/`--full`, while `--output llm` only minifies keys and can retain bodies. The search matcher currently discards match positions, so snippet extraction needs an explicit data path. CLI JSON and MCP need one named search-result schema, with a separately named minified LLM schema. I am revising the plan to define exact fields, 240-character summary/snippet budgets, predicate-only behavior, `--full` migration behavior, tests, and list as out of scope."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786396167603234001,"uuid":"c72ae0f4-a245-4d12-9a4a-96ae5abfff9e"}